WEBVTT

00:01.820 --> 00:06.040
Three years have passed since Sion
the legendary hero sealed the Gates of Hell.

01:54.460 --> 01:56.560
Truly awe-inspiring...

02:02.560 --> 02:04.420
What a gorgeous radish!

02:04.420 --> 02:06.310
You really do have the perfect figure!

02:07.140 --> 02:09.310
I hereby dub you Katherine.

02:09.310 --> 02:11.690
Now, let's dress you up real nice!

02:15.680 --> 02:17.810
Touka! What are you doing?

02:20.610 --> 02:22.120
Y-Yuna?!

02:22.120 --> 02:24.830
I-I'm just harvesting radishes!

02:24.830 --> 02:27.580
So why are you putting a stocking on it?

02:27.580 --> 02:31.340
Upon finding a radish shaped
like the perfect thigh, any man would

02:31.340 --> 02:33.420
feel compelled to put a stocking on it!

02:33.420 --> 02:35.420
You're the only pervert who'd do that!

02:36.730 --> 02:38.070
Honestly!

02:38.070 --> 02:41.100
When you're not lazing around,
you're doing gross stuff like that.

02:41.100 --> 02:43.660
Why'd I have to be childhood friends
with someone like you?

02:43.660 --> 02:44.350
What?

02:44.350 --> 02:46.400
The legendary hero is our age,

02:46.400 --> 02:49.190
and he managed to save the whole world!

02:49.190 --> 02:50.290
Yeah, yeah.

02:50.290 --> 02:53.890
Legendary hero this, legendary hero that.
He's all you people talk about.

02:53.890 --> 02:56.280
The Sacred Sword could've
chosen anyone, you know?

02:56.280 --> 02:58.930
Besides, his seal didn't hold up for long,

02:58.930 --> 03:01.030
and now the devils are back on the loose.

03:01.030 --> 03:04.990
That's why he's traveling
far and wide to slay them all!

03:04.990 --> 03:07.490
Cleaning up after yourself ain't very heroic.

03:07.490 --> 03:09.620
But I don't care what happens far and wide

03:09.620 --> 03:13.130
so long as my own house
and field are safe.

03:14.590 --> 03:16.800
And you too, of course, Yuna.

03:17.620 --> 03:19.360
What's that supposed to mean?

03:19.360 --> 03:24.140
She might be a mean old nag,
but she's got perfect proportions.

03:24.140 --> 03:26.340
Especially those thighs!

03:26.340 --> 03:28.450
Those freaking luscious thighs!

03:30.120 --> 03:31.320
The hell are you doing?!

03:31.320 --> 03:32.690
S-Sorry, force of habit...

03:32.690 --> 03:34.050
Honestly!

03:34.050 --> 03:37.900
The whole world's in peril,
but that's still all you think about!

03:37.900 --> 03:40.820
Devils could even attack here, you know?

03:40.820 --> 03:42.660
Thankfully, I'm prepared for that!

03:44.160 --> 03:45.930
Behold my brilliant trap!

03:45.930 --> 03:48.620
It'll skewer any devils that enter my field!

03:48.620 --> 03:50.440
That's so stupid.

03:50.440 --> 03:51.580
H-Hey...

03:51.580 --> 03:54.360
Why's she always gotta take me down a peg?

03:58.130 --> 04:00.570
I love humans.

04:00.570 --> 04:02.090
I eat humans.

04:02.090 --> 04:03.430
Ah! A devil!

04:03.430 --> 04:05.050
It's a devil attack!

04:07.740 --> 04:10.390
No... S-Stay back...

04:10.390 --> 04:13.350
Human. Woman. Looks tasty.

04:13.350 --> 04:14.690
Yuna!

04:14.690 --> 04:16.070
What do I do?

04:16.070 --> 04:18.710
I need Yuna for my future plans.

04:18.710 --> 04:20.720
I've gotta rescue her somehow.

04:24.300 --> 04:25.610
Oh, Mr. Devil!

04:25.610 --> 04:28.230
I've got some tasty meat grilling here!

04:28.230 --> 04:32.250
Even a devil has to prefer
a well-browned cut of juicy pork!

04:32.250 --> 04:34.100
That's it! C'mon over here!

04:34.100 --> 04:37.130
And fall right into my brilliant trap!

04:37.130 --> 04:40.210
Gross. I hate pork.

04:40.210 --> 04:42.500
So pork isn't gonna do the job...

04:43.430 --> 04:44.390
Crap!

04:44.390 --> 04:47.680
That expression screams,
"Why are you grilling when I'm in danger?!"

04:48.470 --> 04:50.920
Damn it all. I'll have to step in!

04:50.920 --> 04:52.430
Get away from her!

04:55.620 --> 04:56.850
Are you all right?

04:57.400 --> 04:59.820
Th-The legendary hero!

04:59.820 --> 05:01.150
It's the legendary hero!

05:01.150 --> 05:03.780
The legendary hero's here to save us!

05:03.780 --> 05:06.530
Mr. Legendary Hero! Thank you so much!

05:06.530 --> 05:08.410
I'm just glad to see you safe, Miss Yuna.

05:08.410 --> 05:10.990
Y-You remember me?!

05:10.990 --> 05:12.510
Of course I do!

05:12.510 --> 05:14.040
It's been three whole years.

05:14.040 --> 05:15.120
Have you been well?

05:15.120 --> 05:19.590
I forgot this jerk saved
Yuna three years ago too...

05:19.590 --> 05:20.990
I'm so delighted!

05:20.990 --> 05:23.580
I was sure you'd forgotten me!

05:23.580 --> 05:27.020
The delight's all mine,
since I get to see you happy again.

05:27.020 --> 05:29.810
I just love your smile, you know.

05:30.430 --> 05:32.140
Oh, Mr. Legendary Hero...

05:32.140 --> 05:35.310
"I just love your smile," he says?!

05:35.310 --> 05:37.810
This piece-of-shit hero is one smooth talker!

05:38.220 --> 05:39.980
And Yuna's lapping it up!

05:39.980 --> 05:41.820
Hey, Yuna! I also tried to save—

05:41.820 --> 05:44.060
Stay out of this, scumbag.

05:44.060 --> 05:46.280
Go back to your one-man barbecue.

05:46.280 --> 05:48.290
What's with the total one-eighty?!

05:48.290 --> 05:50.740
I like you better smiling too, you know!

05:50.740 --> 05:54.330
After three years, Yuna was
finally warming up to me!

05:54.330 --> 05:56.290
This is all that hero's fault!

05:57.460 --> 05:59.660
What's that sound? Another devil?!

05:59.660 --> 06:00.920
I'm sorry.

06:00.920 --> 06:03.130
I'm afraid that's my stomach rumbling.

06:04.590 --> 06:07.810
W-Would you like to come by my house, then?

06:07.810 --> 06:09.980
I made a bit too much for lunch...

06:09.980 --> 06:10.890
Really?

06:10.890 --> 06:13.100
He gets to eat Yuna's home cooking?!

06:13.100 --> 06:15.140
Not even I've had that!

06:15.140 --> 06:16.600
Now they're just rubbing it in...

06:18.890 --> 06:21.270
Is that barbecue I smell?

06:21.270 --> 06:23.560
I just love meat! I—

06:29.430 --> 06:30.530
You gotta be kiddin' me...

06:30.530 --> 06:32.990
No!

06:33.560 --> 06:36.700
Th-There's no way the guy
who saved the world just...

06:37.600 --> 06:38.660
Yeah, he's dead.

06:38.660 --> 06:40.270
How can this be?!

06:40.270 --> 06:43.980
Without the legendary hero,
we can't seal the Gates of Hell!

06:43.980 --> 06:46.460
What a nightmare! It's the end of humanity!

06:46.460 --> 06:50.000
We should put Touka on trial
before His Majesty!

06:50.000 --> 06:51.280
Now hold on a minute!

06:51.280 --> 06:52.540
This was an accident.

06:52.540 --> 06:56.860
Besides, I'm the victim here.
He was trespassing to steal food.

06:57.890 --> 06:59.310
Don't make excuses!

06:59.310 --> 07:00.820
You can atone with your life!

07:00.820 --> 07:02.100
Ch-Chill out!

07:02.480 --> 07:04.730
Let's think about this calmly for a moment.

07:04.730 --> 07:06.890
The legendary hero died
falling into a trap...

07:06.890 --> 07:08.440
Who'd even believe that story?

07:09.640 --> 07:12.030
If a buncha villagers came
to <i>me</i> with that,

07:12.030 --> 07:14.300
I'd bet <i>they</i> were the ones who did it!

07:14.300 --> 07:17.550
You're gonna try to pin this on us?!

07:17.550 --> 07:19.460
No... I'm afraid he has a point.

07:19.460 --> 07:22.650
No one would believe he died like this.

07:23.210 --> 07:25.180
W-We could blame it on a devil...

07:25.180 --> 07:28.050
Then how do we explain how <i>we</i> survived?

07:28.050 --> 07:30.220
But what other choice do we have?

07:30.220 --> 07:31.260
Hold it.

07:31.260 --> 07:33.220
There <i>is</i> another option.

07:35.470 --> 07:37.760
Now, as far as anyone knows,
he's just missing.

07:37.760 --> 07:39.180
We had no part in it.

07:40.140 --> 07:41.880
"No part in it," my butt...

07:41.880 --> 07:45.160
Guess it figures that it takes
a madman to off the legendary hero.

07:45.160 --> 07:46.440
What do you want me to do?!

07:46.440 --> 07:48.400
All our asses are on the line here!

07:48.770 --> 07:51.220
We're just protecting the village.

07:58.830 --> 08:01.370
Man, I feel great this morning.

08:01.370 --> 08:05.230
Hiding the legendary hero's corpse
must've been really therapeutic.

08:05.230 --> 08:07.230
I feel like a whole new man—

08:09.480 --> 08:10.440
What's going on?

08:10.440 --> 08:11.920
I look like the legendary hero!

08:12.530 --> 08:14.680
And on his worst day, no less...

08:14.680 --> 08:16.700
Maybe I'm dreaming.

08:17.910 --> 08:20.140
Who could it be at this early hour?

08:21.230 --> 08:22.580
Mr. Legendary Hero?!

08:23.130 --> 08:25.910
Mr. Legendary Hero, you came back to life?!

08:25.910 --> 08:27.980
W-Well, actually...

08:27.980 --> 08:30.530
I guess I do look just like him.

08:30.530 --> 08:33.360
Damn it, why'd I end up with that jerk's mug?

08:33.950 --> 08:36.520
Hang on, she's totally into me!

08:36.520 --> 08:38.280
That's it! At last, I could...

08:38.280 --> 08:41.360
Well, Yuna, I had a favor to ask you...

08:42.160 --> 08:46.210
Will this serve your purpose,
Mr. Legendary Hero?

08:46.210 --> 08:48.170
Th-This is...

08:48.170 --> 08:49.790
The power of the legendary hero!

08:49.790 --> 08:51.850
The power of the world's savior!

08:51.850 --> 08:57.140
Now I can put stockings on the luscious
thighs of beautiful girls the world over!

08:58.300 --> 09:02.390
The legendary hero is looking at me
with the most piercing gaze...

09:02.790 --> 09:04.290
He really is wonderful!

09:04.290 --> 09:05.930
Nothing like that stupid Touka!

09:05.930 --> 09:08.330
Though he does smell a little rank...

09:08.330 --> 09:10.200
No, don't say that, Yuna!

09:10.200 --> 09:12.230
Even if he stinks, the legendary hero...

09:12.230 --> 09:13.450
Stinks!

09:14.030 --> 09:16.220
Mr. Legendary Hero,
you reek to hell and back!

09:16.220 --> 09:17.550
Calm down, Yuna!

09:17.550 --> 09:18.710
What are you—

09:20.200 --> 09:21.030
Huh?

09:21.030 --> 09:22.200
You monster!

09:22.200 --> 09:24.330
N-No! I'm Touka!

09:24.330 --> 09:26.420
Touka's no monster!

09:26.420 --> 09:28.580
I just woke up like this!

09:28.580 --> 09:30.630
Oh? Prove you're Touka, then!

09:30.630 --> 09:32.460
Magical Girl Magical Yunarin.

09:33.630 --> 09:37.550
That's what you called yourself at age
twelve when you wanted to be a mage.

09:38.010 --> 09:40.260
I'm the only one in the village who knows.

09:40.260 --> 09:43.040
You even made that lame outfit
you were so proud of!

09:43.040 --> 09:44.730
It was hilarious.

09:44.730 --> 09:46.450
Huh? Yunarin?

09:46.450 --> 09:47.310
Yunari—

09:48.300 --> 09:51.020
Fine, we've established that you're Touka.

09:51.020 --> 09:53.820
So, how did you turn into the legendary hero?

09:53.820 --> 09:56.900
No idea. I wish I knew.

09:56.900 --> 10:02.080
Seems like my soul got swapped
into his buried corpse,

10:02.080 --> 10:04.290
so it must be magic at work.

10:06.120 --> 10:07.890
So you recognized my necromancy!

10:07.890 --> 10:10.570
As expected of the man
who killed Sion the hero!

10:10.570 --> 10:11.560
Who's there?!

10:12.860 --> 10:14.710
It's coming from your field.

10:16.180 --> 10:17.420
It's about time!

10:17.950 --> 10:21.300
I'm Anri Haysworth the necromancer!

10:21.300 --> 10:25.020
The one who made you Sion the hero!

10:28.140 --> 10:30.560
And why did you do that, huh?!

10:30.560 --> 10:31.520
You're still going?!

10:31.970 --> 10:34.860
W-Well... I...

10:34.860 --> 10:38.320
B-Before I answer, could you please help me?

10:39.790 --> 10:41.530
That was a close call!

10:43.090 --> 10:48.640
I was dying to see how you'd react when you
woke up looking like the legendary hero...

10:50.540 --> 10:54.250
To think you'd anticipate
my actions and set a trap!

10:54.250 --> 10:56.000
Sounds like you just screwed up to me!

10:56.290 --> 10:58.580
I know jack about necromancers,

10:58.580 --> 11:01.320
but I got better things to do
than entertain a child's prank.

11:01.320 --> 11:02.680
So go on. Turn me back.

11:02.680 --> 11:04.100
This is no prank!

11:04.100 --> 11:08.060
You must now save the world
as the legendary hero!

11:08.060 --> 11:09.020
What?

11:09.020 --> 11:13.110
When I was traveling with
Sion the hero, I made him a promise...

11:13.520 --> 11:16.040
If it ever seems my death is imminent,

11:16.040 --> 11:20.070
I want you to use your power
to bequeath my body to another.

11:20.430 --> 11:23.660
Someone you believe can save the world.

11:24.090 --> 11:28.710
Not only did you kill Sion,
you nearly managed to get me too!

11:28.710 --> 11:32.720
Someone of your prowess
can surely save the world!

11:32.720 --> 11:34.710
You both just fell in, damn it!

11:35.420 --> 11:37.840
Okay, I get it now.

11:37.840 --> 11:38.880
In that case...

11:39.720 --> 11:40.810
I'm coming with!

11:40.810 --> 11:42.010
You sure packed fast!

11:42.010 --> 11:45.420
I've always wanted to go on an adventure.

11:45.420 --> 11:48.970
I've got to repay the legendary
hero for saving me...

11:48.970 --> 11:51.470
And you've got to make up for what you did!

11:51.830 --> 11:53.690
Sounds dumb. Pass.

11:53.690 --> 11:58.650
Oh? You'd rather be punished
for killing the hero instead?

11:59.260 --> 12:01.960
Then I'll put you to death, here and now!

12:01.960 --> 12:04.590
I-I'm still in the hero's body.

12:04.590 --> 12:05.870
A li'l punk like you can't—

12:05.870 --> 12:09.280
Your original body is still your true form.

12:10.760 --> 12:13.520
This is the Coffin of the Living,
an ancient magic artifact.

12:13.520 --> 12:16.920
Your original body is sealed within.

12:16.920 --> 12:19.510
The moment I destroy it,

12:19.510 --> 12:22.630
your consciousness will expire.

12:23.540 --> 12:25.090
I see.

12:25.820 --> 12:27.450
If that's how you wanna play...

12:28.330 --> 12:30.450
Please, let me save the world.

12:30.450 --> 12:31.430
Very good!

12:33.180 --> 12:35.520
Wow! What a bustling town!

12:35.520 --> 12:38.430
Bellun is the largest city in the region.

12:38.430 --> 12:40.730
We'll prepare for our journey here.

12:41.580 --> 12:43.370
You can prepare all you want.

12:43.370 --> 12:45.610
I'm still not psychologically ready.

12:45.610 --> 12:48.740
Man up and face facts already, would you?

12:48.740 --> 12:52.890
Ha! I can't change my emotions
on a whim like you do.

12:52.890 --> 12:56.740
Acting like some tourist right
after your beloved hero died...

12:56.740 --> 12:58.560
Talk about heartless.

12:58.560 --> 13:00.210
I'm still totally sad about that!

13:00.210 --> 13:04.610
But the legendary hero said he loved my smile,

13:04.610 --> 13:06.930
so I can't stay down in the dumps forever.

13:06.930 --> 13:09.130
Huh, you don't say.

13:09.130 --> 13:13.450
Meanwhile, I'll be smile-free until
this whole stupid journey's over.

13:13.450 --> 13:15.140
Look! It's the legendary hero!

13:15.500 --> 13:17.690
What a dreamboat!

13:17.690 --> 13:19.110
He's so handsome!

13:19.110 --> 13:21.730
This body freaking rocks!

13:23.190 --> 13:25.460
Look at these cute wands!

13:25.460 --> 13:27.070
I kinda want one.

13:27.070 --> 13:30.450
As I'd expect of the hero's companion,
you have a discerning eye.

13:30.450 --> 13:34.350
That's our best magic catalyst.

13:34.350 --> 13:35.160
Really?

13:35.490 --> 13:37.570
You can't even use magic.

13:37.570 --> 13:40.130
So what? I can get the look down first.

13:40.420 --> 13:41.510
If you insist.

13:41.510 --> 13:43.710
I'll buy it for you as a gift.

13:43.710 --> 13:44.980
Touka...

13:44.980 --> 13:46.800
Shopkeep, how much for the wand?

13:46.800 --> 13:49.010
Ten million kruks.

13:49.010 --> 13:52.580
W-Wow, only ten million?

13:52.580 --> 13:54.420
Anri, how much does the hero's party have?

13:54.420 --> 13:56.350
Not that much, for sure.

13:58.660 --> 14:01.150
Would you two mind waiting outside?

14:03.690 --> 14:05.530
He gave it to me for a thousand.

14:05.530 --> 14:06.110
What?!

14:06.110 --> 14:07.770
How'd you manage that?

14:07.770 --> 14:10.070
With charisma that exceeds
the legendary hero's.

14:10.810 --> 14:15.040
This is all we have, and it won't buy
much more than a room for the night.

14:15.040 --> 14:16.510
What gives, Anri?

14:16.510 --> 14:20.050
Didn't the king pay you
a reward three years ago?

14:20.050 --> 14:21.260
Nope.

14:21.260 --> 14:23.940
I've never even met the king.

14:23.940 --> 14:25.510
Huh? How come?

14:25.510 --> 14:28.740
Is that because necromancy
is taboo or something?

14:29.260 --> 14:30.270
Y-Yes...

14:30.270 --> 14:31.340
I thought so.

14:31.340 --> 14:33.180
What's a taboo?

14:33.180 --> 14:36.300
A kind of magic that's illegal to even use.

14:36.300 --> 14:39.540
If it gets out that she's a taboo-caster,

14:39.540 --> 14:41.650
she could be executed for it.

14:41.650 --> 14:42.700
Indeed.

14:42.700 --> 14:48.010
Only our party at the time knows I was
a part of what happened three years ago.

14:48.010 --> 14:52.620
Even at your village, I simply watched
from afar so as not to make trouble.

14:53.020 --> 14:55.580
What will we do for our
upcoming journey, then?

14:55.580 --> 14:57.960
Leave it to my charisma.

15:03.560 --> 15:05.080
Our meal's on the house!

15:05.080 --> 15:06.300
No way!

15:06.300 --> 15:09.550
Man, I'm thinking we can do this
without any money at all!

15:09.550 --> 15:11.510
That's the man who defeated the hero for you!

15:11.510 --> 15:14.400
You want us to keep relying
on people's goodwill?

15:14.400 --> 15:16.150
We'll be leeches on society!

15:16.150 --> 15:18.060
Yes, indeed. That's very true!

15:18.060 --> 15:19.800
Then what are we supposed to do?

15:19.800 --> 15:22.510
Let's look for work at the adventurers' guild.

15:23.170 --> 15:25.010
You want to take honest work?

15:25.010 --> 15:27.040
Well, I think that's a terrible—

15:27.040 --> 15:28.490
Mr. Legendary Hero!

15:30.020 --> 15:32.360
Older ladies with luscious thighs!

15:32.360 --> 15:35.370
Want to come by and <i>sample our wares</i>?

15:35.370 --> 15:37.790
You kind of stink, though,
Mr. Legendary Hero...

15:37.790 --> 15:42.530
N-Not many chances to
wash up on a long journey!

15:42.530 --> 15:45.750
Oh! Why don't you clean up with us, then?

15:45.750 --> 15:48.890
You know, I've never met the real hero,

15:48.890 --> 15:52.080
and I hear there've been lots
of impostors lately.

15:52.510 --> 15:55.140
Why don't we ask my bodyguard about it?

15:55.140 --> 15:57.820
He said he fought
alongside him once, after all!

15:59.800 --> 16:02.890
He does look like the real deal.

16:02.890 --> 16:05.170
I'm honored to meet you again!

16:05.170 --> 16:07.800
Do you remember the promise
you made me that day?

16:07.800 --> 16:08.780
Promise?

16:08.780 --> 16:11.380
I requested a proper duel.

16:11.380 --> 16:13.990
I'm willing to die here if I have to.

16:13.990 --> 16:16.320
Can't say I feel the same, personally!

16:16.320 --> 16:18.190
Go, Mr. Legendary Hero!

16:18.190 --> 16:20.310
Win, and we can all take a bath together!

16:20.310 --> 16:23.020
There's no plausible way I can win...

16:23.600 --> 16:26.200
Wait, the hero has the Sacred Sword!

16:26.200 --> 16:29.500
With this, there's no way I can lose!

16:29.500 --> 16:31.300
I'll end this in a minute flat.

16:34.340 --> 16:36.300
I'm so limber in this body!

16:36.300 --> 16:38.510
I'll show you what the hero can really do!

16:40.370 --> 16:41.120
Huh?

16:43.310 --> 16:45.520
My eye! My eye!

16:45.520 --> 16:48.190
Why'd the Sacred Sword bend like that?!

16:49.490 --> 16:50.870
He's a fake!

16:50.870 --> 16:53.030
The legendary hero's nowhere near that weak!

16:53.900 --> 16:57.370
I knew something smelled about this.

16:59.730 --> 17:00.830
Honestly!

17:00.830 --> 17:03.080
Where'd that stupid Touka run off to?

17:03.080 --> 17:05.460
Miss Yuna! What about this job?

17:06.250 --> 17:08.670
Eliminating devils? And each one's worth...

17:08.670 --> 17:10.380
Three hundred thousand?!

17:10.380 --> 17:12.990
We can slay devils <i>and</i> earn money!

17:12.990 --> 17:14.870
Two birds with one stone!

17:15.900 --> 17:17.370
Now shower me with praise!

17:17.370 --> 17:19.340
Of course! What a smart girl!

17:19.340 --> 17:21.470
Anri? Is that you?

17:22.430 --> 17:23.400
Who's that?

17:23.400 --> 17:24.560
Someone you know?

17:24.560 --> 17:26.400
I'm Kyle.

17:26.400 --> 17:29.270
I worked with Anri to save the world.

17:29.270 --> 17:32.830
<i>The</i> Kyle? The scion of one of the continent's
most prestigious families

17:32.830 --> 17:37.490
who made a name for himself as
the legendary hero's right-hand man?

17:38.910 --> 17:42.450
I'm sure you're intimidated
by my noble status,

17:42.450 --> 17:44.870
but feel free to treat me like anyone else.

17:44.870 --> 17:47.830
What brings you
to a place like this, Sir Kyle?

17:48.180 --> 17:51.290
I've been trying to track sightings of Sion.

17:51.710 --> 17:55.180
But I suppose you know where he is, right?

17:55.180 --> 17:56.860
The legendary hero...

17:56.860 --> 17:58.000
is dead.

17:59.270 --> 18:01.020
Return my ten-million-kruk wand!

18:01.020 --> 18:03.220
Pay up, you damn fake!

18:03.220 --> 18:06.310
Take a close look!
I'm really the legendary hero!

18:06.310 --> 18:09.670
The hero doesn't look
that sickly or smell that bad!

18:09.670 --> 18:10.980
Well, see, there was this curse, and...
Yeah, he's right!

18:10.980 --> 18:12.520
Well, see, there was this curse, and...

18:12.900 --> 18:14.120
Stupid Anri!

18:14.120 --> 18:18.280
You said my mana would automatically
restore my zombified body!

18:18.280 --> 18:20.740
But I'm obviously rotting!

18:21.520 --> 18:23.840
Plus, I've got the Sacred—

18:24.700 --> 18:29.670
Replicas I've confiscated
from impostors like you.

18:29.670 --> 18:34.000
To discourage further copycats, we should
make an example of you with a life sentence.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.970
Maybe a death sentence would be more apt.

18:35.970 --> 18:37.320
Hell no, it wouldn't!

18:37.320 --> 18:39.380
I implore you to wait.

18:39.900 --> 18:41.110
Lord Kyle?!

18:41.110 --> 18:42.930
The legendary hero's companion?

18:42.930 --> 18:44.590
Well, well! Lord Kyle!

18:44.590 --> 18:45.950
What brings you here?

18:45.950 --> 18:47.900
I have business with an old friend.

18:47.900 --> 18:50.170
He's the real deal. I'd like him released.

18:50.170 --> 18:55.200
Please, my lord. His appearance and
behavior suggest quite the contrary...

18:55.200 --> 18:57.370
Shall I show you the proof?

18:59.390 --> 19:01.040
You saved me!

19:01.040 --> 19:02.980
Anri filled me in on the situation.

19:02.980 --> 19:06.200
Hold the Sacred Sword
and visualize a giant blade.

19:06.200 --> 19:08.160
A giant blade?

19:11.520 --> 19:12.630
What the hell?!

19:12.630 --> 19:15.090
That's the true Sacred Sword!

19:15.090 --> 19:18.500
When we fought together, his sword
would swell to massive proportions

19:18.500 --> 19:20.800
and he'd nail the devils all at once!

19:20.800 --> 19:21.720
That means this man is the real—
I've seen it too!

19:21.720 --> 19:23.260
Me too!
That means this man is the real—

19:24.090 --> 19:24.930
It's drooping.

19:24.930 --> 19:25.790
It wasn't bendy when I saw him fight...

19:25.790 --> 19:27.390
What now?
It wasn't bendy when I saw him fight...

19:27.390 --> 19:29.350
What the hell is that?
Maybe he <i>is</i> a fake?

19:29.710 --> 19:31.840
It seems that he is a fake, after—

19:31.840 --> 19:33.060
Hold it right there!

19:33.060 --> 19:36.760
If he slays more devils
on this quest than anyone,

19:36.760 --> 19:38.400
that'll prove it, right?

19:38.400 --> 19:40.740
Wait, hang on. That seems kinda—

19:40.740 --> 19:42.200
Yeah!

19:42.960 --> 19:44.150
Interesting.

19:44.150 --> 19:47.580
Let us have him prove himself, then.

19:48.030 --> 19:51.040
Over twenty devils have been sighted?!

19:51.040 --> 19:52.750
I don't stand a damn chance!

19:52.750 --> 19:54.200
What do you want from me?!

19:54.200 --> 19:57.050
This was the only way
to get them off your back!

19:57.050 --> 20:00.510
Sir Touka, all journeys contain trials.

20:00.510 --> 20:02.080
And also,

20:02.080 --> 20:04.970
I wanna know why I'm rotting
and my sword went flaccid.

20:06.140 --> 20:07.220
I see.

20:07.220 --> 20:11.230
The chosen one's mana determines
the Sacred Sword's strength.

20:11.230 --> 20:14.810
You'll also require mana
to maintain that zombie body.

20:14.810 --> 20:17.650
This leads me to one conclusion...

20:17.650 --> 20:21.070
You have a miserably limited amount of mana.

20:21.070 --> 20:23.250
But I'm in the legendary hero's body now!

20:23.250 --> 20:26.780
Nay, mana derives from the spirit.

20:26.780 --> 20:27.780
That makes sense.

20:27.780 --> 20:31.770
Touka's worthless soul
means he has piddly mana.

20:31.770 --> 20:32.860
I was careless...

20:32.860 --> 20:36.580
I assumed the man who slew the hero
would have plenty of mana!

20:36.580 --> 20:40.210
M-Maybe it went flaccid
because I'm <i>too</i> awesome!

20:40.210 --> 20:41.420
In that case...

20:41.420 --> 20:43.310
This is a magic crystal.

20:43.310 --> 20:46.010
They're typically used in spellcasting,

20:46.010 --> 20:47.950
but if you grip one tightly,

20:48.470 --> 20:52.380
it will shine according to the holder's mana.

20:52.380 --> 20:55.130
That light suggests
the highest possible level.

20:55.910 --> 20:57.130
Hand it over.

21:01.040 --> 21:02.610
I don't think it's working.

21:02.610 --> 21:03.570
No...

21:03.570 --> 21:05.380
There's a faint light in the center.

21:05.380 --> 21:06.260
Sad.

21:06.260 --> 21:07.200
Very well...

21:07.200 --> 21:11.200
Sir Touka has a mana level of 1,
akin to a baby's.

21:11.200 --> 21:13.110
What about mine?!

21:13.110 --> 21:16.040
Yours is level 2, akin to a child's.

21:16.040 --> 21:17.210
No way!

21:17.210 --> 21:20.080
This is a rather grave turn of events.

21:20.080 --> 21:21.770
It's bad enough to be a poor combatant,

21:21.770 --> 21:25.010
but at this rate, you'll just keep rotting
until you're a mere skeleton.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.470
Thus, I propose...

21:26.470 --> 21:29.930
Why not let me play
the legendary hero instead?

21:29.930 --> 21:32.010
That's a great idea!

21:32.010 --> 21:34.120
Then I can go back to my body!

21:34.120 --> 21:36.910
He'd be a million times
better at it than Touka!

21:36.910 --> 21:37.900
No!

21:37.900 --> 21:40.860
I won't accept Sir Kyle
as the legendary hero.

21:40.860 --> 21:44.610
But shouldn't the job go to
the guy who wants it?

21:44.610 --> 21:47.640
You're still angry about three years ago?

21:47.640 --> 21:49.770
Did something happen back then?

21:49.770 --> 21:51.330
No. That is unrelated.

21:51.330 --> 21:55.220
The legendary hero's successor must be
capable of saving the world.

21:55.220 --> 21:56.960
One of you managed to slay him.

21:56.960 --> 21:59.010
The other could never best him.

21:59.010 --> 22:00.550
If I must gamble, I choose the former.

22:00.550 --> 22:02.170
Seriously, it was an accident!

22:02.170 --> 22:03.420
In that case...

22:04.590 --> 22:08.050
If I slay him now, will you accept me then?

22:08.940 --> 22:10.050
Huh?!
